usage: PROGRAM [--backend wayland|x11|win32] [--frames N] [--screenshot out.ppm] [--no-vsync] [--validation]
       [--inject-device-loss FRAME] [--inject-oom N] [--gpu ID|INDEX|NAME] [--list-gpus]
  --backend B       display backend (default: automatic; same as ENGINE_WINDOW_BACKEND)
  --frames N        stop after N frames (also RHI_DEMO_FRAMES=N)
  --screenshot P    render offscreen, no window, and write the last frame to P (a binary PPM)
  --no-vsync        present without waiting for the display
  --gpu G           the GPU to use: an id from --list-gpus, an index, or part of the name
  --list-gpus       print the GPUs and exit
  --validation      enable the validation layer with synchronization validation
  --inject-device-loss F  fault injection: lose the GPU device at frame F (exit code 3)
  --inject-oom N    fault injection: fail device-memory allocation number N and every one after it
Settings:
  --set KEY=VALUE         set a setting (repeatable; the value may be quoted); --list-settings shows the keys
  --settings FILE         read settings from FILE (above the project file, below the environment)
  --save-settings[=FILE]  write the settings that differ from their defaults to FILE (default: the user's settings file) and exit
  --list-settings         print every setting: its value, default, where it came from and what it is for, and exit
  --backend NAME          platform.window_backend: the display backend: wayland or x11 on Linux, win32 on Windows (auto picks Wayland, then X11, on Linux)
  --gpu TEXT              renderer.adapter: the GPU: an id from --list-gpus, an index, or part of the name (empty: the best one)
  --rhi NAME              renderer.backend: the graphics backend: auto (the preferred one this program has and this machine runs), null (no GPU), vulkan or dx12
Environment: ENGINE_SETTING_<KEY> sets any setting (the key in capitals, dots written as __, e.g. ENGINE_SETTING_RENDERER__PRESENT_MODE); also:
  ENGINE_WINDOW_BACKEND                 platform.window_backend
  ENGINE_RHI_GPU                        renderer.adapter
  ENGINE_RHI_VALIDATION_SYNC            renderer.sync_validation
  ENGINE_RHI_CACHE_DIR                  rhi.pipeline_cache_dir
